## V8 gate-fix session (round 12): root-cause fix for the recurring `.jdone` parity conflict

## What changed

### `src/server/routes/events.ts` (new, 233 lines)

Read-only module over the durable event log built by O1/O3. Exports
`EVENT_STREAM_HEARTBEAT_MS = 10_000`, `EventStreamDeps` (`heartbeatMs`, `pollMs`, `now`),
`streamFrame(ev)` and `handleEventsRoutes(req, res, p, deps)`.

- `GET /api/sessions/:id/events?after_seq=0&limit=500` -> `{ data, next_after_seq, has_more }`.
  `limit` is clamped to 1..5000. `after` and `afterSeq` are tolerated as aliases for
  `after_seq`. Rows come from the O1 log and are returned in ascending `seq`.
- `GET /api/sessions/:id/events/stream` -> `text/event-stream`. The handler writes a
  `retry:` line, an initial `resume` frame carrying the cursor it will use, then polls
  the log for rows with `seq > afterSeq` and emits one SSE frame per row.
  - Resume: `?after_seq=` wins over the `Last-Event-ID` header; a header value that is
    not a positive integer is ignored rather than throwing.
  - Every event frame carries `id: <seq>` (the durable sequence), so a reconnect that
    sends that value back resumes exactly.
  - Heartbeat: a `: hb` comment is written at least every `EVENT_STREAM_HEARTBEAT_MS`
    (10 s) while the stream is idle or waiting, so a proxy cannot drop an idle
    connection before new events arrive.
- `streamFrame(ev)` special-cases `kind === "chat_event"`: the stored payload already is
  the section 8 socket envelope, so it is returned as `{ ...envelope, seq: ev.seq }`
  (spread plus the durable `seq` added, not a byte-for-byte passthrough). Every other
  `kind` is rendered as `{ id, type: "event", sessionId, timestamp, seq, kind, event }`.
  So rows of every kind are still delivered, and the client can tell a replayed chat
  frame from another kind by `kind`. `LogKind` is
  `"input" | "chat_event" | "tool_result" | "checkpoint" | "status"`; this module names
  only `chat_event` explicitly and routes any other kind through the generic arm.

No writer was added to this module. Reads go only through the O1 log
(`src/protocol/eventLog.ts`), importing `after as afterSeq` and `headSeq`; the module
imports nothing from the O3 adapter (`src/protocol/store.ts`). Nothing here writes to or
bypasses the durable store.

### `src/server/http.ts` (3 lines)

- Imports `handleEventsRoutes` from `./routes/events.js`.
- Dispatches the two routes after `handleSessionRuntimeRoutes` and before
  `handleDesignStudioRoutes`, so they sit inside the same `/api` dispatch chain and reuse
  the existing JSON/SSE plumbing rather than adding a second mount point. They are behind
  the general install-token check in the dispatcher's async IIFE (`http.ts` ~L446-468:
  `validateLocalToken` unless `LOAM_AUTH_DISABLED === "true"`), the same gate every other
  `/api` route gets. There is no per-route auth in this module and no new gate was added.

## Acceptance criteria (plan row O8)

| Acceptance | Covered by |
|---|---|
| Last-Event-ID resume returns only the missing events | `HTTP resume returns only the missing events` (cursor `after_seq=3` yields exactly seq 4-6) and `resumes an SSE stream from Last-Event-ID and sends only the missing events` (header `last-event-id: 2` replays exactly seq 3-5 and the `resume` frame echoes `after_seq: 2`); `resumes the SSE stream over the wire and carries the seq as the frame id` repeats it against the real server. `prefers ?after_seq over Last-Event-ID` and `streams only newly appended events after the resume cursor` pin cursor precedence and the live tail |
| SSE heartbeat at least every 10 s | `sends a heartbeat comment at most 10 s apart` drives the stream with a 300 ms stand-in cadence (`heartbeatMs: 300`) and asserts `>= 3` `: hb` comments flow, then asserts the shipped `EVENT_STREAM_HEARTBEAT_MS === 10_000` and `<= 10_000`. It does not wait a real 10 s. `caps a requested heartbeat at the 10 s ceiling` asserts a `heartbeatMs: 60_000` request is clamped so `retry:` equals `EVENT_STREAM_HEARTBEAT_MS` |
| every SSE frame carries `id: <seq>` | `encodes the frame id as the event seq and forwards a chat envelope verbatim` asserts `frame.id === ev.seq` for both the generic and `chat_event` arms (the test's own name keeps the word "verbatim"; the assertion is only on the frame `id` and the payload shape, not on byte identity, since the `chat_event` arm stamps `seq` onto a spread copy); `resumes an SSE stream from Last-Event-ID ...` asserts the parsed `id:` lines (`sseIds`) are exactly the replayed seqs, and the real-server test repeats it over the wire |

## Tests

`src/server/__tests__/eventsRoutes.test.ts` (new, 13 tests / 2 suites, all pass):

- A `FakeResponse` (Writable) plus a `callRoutes` helper: the handler is typed against
  `ServerResponse`, so the helper casts the fake. `parseSse` tracks `id:` lines
  separately in `sseIds`, because the JSON payload also has an `id` field.
- SSE tests use `openStream` + `runStream(res, writing, until, timeout)`: the handler
  awaits the live tail forever, so the test destroys the response to end it. Seeding uses
  the section 8 mock rows and `append(..., { id: `evt_${sessionId}_${i}` })`, because the
  log's `id` column is globally unique.
- The last block boots the **real** `http.ts` dispatcher via `startServer()` on a
  loopback port (`LOAM_CONFIG` temp, `LOAM_AUTH_DISABLED=true`) and exercises both routes
  over the wire, proving the mount line resolves. It runs with `LOAM_AUTH_DISABLED=true`,
  so it does **not** exercise the install-token gate: `keeps the routes behind the install
  token like the rest of /api` sends a wrong `x-loam-local-token` and expects 200 (gate
  disabled for the suite), then asserts an unknown `/api` path is 404, i.e. that the route
  is dispatched through the same chain. Gate behaviour itself is inherited from `http.ts`,
  not asserted here.
- Imports `../../test/isolation.js` **first** so `config.ts` evaluates after `DATA_DIR`
  is redirected (ESM hoists static imports; the trap is documented in
  `src/test/isolation.ts`). `after()` calls `closeDb()` + `cleanupIsolatedDataDir()`.

Test command:
  node --import tsx --test src/server/__tests__/eventsRoutes.test.ts

