H2 gate-fix session: merge with manus-parity, all gates green

`.jgatefail.txt` reported: `MERGE CONFLICT with latest manus-parity: run git merge
manus-parity, resolve all conflicts keeping both sides, commit.`

## Root cause
The only conflicted file was the tracked rollup marker `.jdone`. Both sides prepended a
new report at the same top-of-file anchor (H2 on this branch; O1, then V11, then D15 on
manus-parity), so git could not auto-merge the two additions. No source file conflicted:
the H2 deliverables (`src/learning/harness/experienceStore.ts` +
`src/learning/harness/__tests__/experienceStore.test.ts`, commit `446de33`) were
already committed and present, and the O1 deliverables (`src/protocol/eventLog.ts` +
`src/protocol/__tests__/eventLog.test.ts`, commit `83b6b8a`) came in from parity.

## What was done
One merge, `git merge manus-parity` (parity tip `b073763`, O1). Three conflict hunks in
`.jdone`; each was resolved by keeping BOTH sides in full (the H2 report header + body and
the O1/D15/V11/rollup reports are all present). No source file was edited, no test was
weakened, deleted or skipped, and no code was dropped.

Verified mechanically that the resolved `.jdone` is a **superset of both conflict sides**:
`git diff --no-index` between each stage-2/stage-3 blob and the working file produced zero
`<` lines (nothing dropped from either side). No conflict markers remain in the tree.

The worktree also carried a spurious `modified: src/agent/masterPromptText.ts` flag that
was purely a stat/CRLF artifact: `git hash-object` of the working file equals the HEAD
blob (`f4efd8e8`), so `git add` produced no staged content change and the flag cleared.

## Gate condition verified
`git merge manus-parity` reports "Already up to date.", `git merge-base --is-ancestor
manus-parity HEAD` exits 0, and `git rev-list --left-right --count manus-parity...HEAD` is
`0  3` (parity fully merged, zero parity commits missing). The tree is clean.

