# J1 gate fix: restore the two corrupted slide scripts and the deleted done-markers.

`.jgatefail.txt` reported a `tsc` failure (TS2451 redeclared block-scoped variables,
TS2300 duplicate identifier) in `src/scripts/check-slide-layouts.ts` and
`src/scripts/check-slide-text-import.ts`. Root cause: the working tree carried
uncommitted edits from a concurrent workstream that had DUPLICATED lines inside those
two files (a bad-merge artifact), and `.jdone` / `.jcode-done` had been deleted from the
working tree. No test was weakened; the fix restores the exact committed blobs.

## What was wrong (and the fix)
- `src/scripts/check-slide-layouts.ts`: `import ExcelJS from 'exceljs';` appeared twice
  (line 1 + line 3), and the whole table/image test block (19 lines) was duplicated
  verbatim (lines 43-61 repeated after line 42). Restored to the committed blob
  (`git diff --exit-code` clean, 43 lines).
- `src/scripts/check-slide-text-import.ts`: `import {renderSlidePreview} ...` appeared
  twice, and the `/api/studio/slide-preview` handler, the `.office-native-ready` wait +
  click + opacity assert, the `.office-native-status` wait, and the `const data = ...`
  preview block were each duplicated inside the single long line 11. Restored to the
  committed blob (`git diff --exit-code` clean, 10 lines).
- `.jdone` and `.jcode-done` (both tracked) were deleted from the working tree; restored
  with `git checkout -- .jdone .jcode-done` (both now tracked, unmodified, no conflict
  markers).

No source logic changed: both scripts are byte-identical to `HEAD` (verified with
`git diff --exit-code`). No test was weakened, deleted or skipped.

