N2 - Canvas view: DONE. Third session (adversarial validation + a real wiring fix)

## What this session changed (source fix, not only a report)
The first report claimed "no source file was edited". This second session found
and fixed a real production bug that the acceptance tests could not see.

### The bug: the canvas node detail never received the chat events
`CanvasPanel` declares `events?: ChatEvent[]` and its `NodeDetail` sheet
renders a "Recent tools" list from it, but the canvas `Editor` wrapper never
forwarded the prop. The shell did wire the events:

- `TaskPageClient.tsx` mounts `<WorkspacePanel ... events={events} />`.
- `WorkspacePanel` already read `events` (it uses them for the header's
  "Running {tool}" line) but passed only `file`, `live`, `onSave` and
  `onChatEdit` to the mounted editor.

So the panel always received `events = []` in the real app and the node detail
showed no "Recent tools" list. The panel's own test still passed because it
injects the events directly into `CanvasPanel`, bypassing the wrapper: the
test exercised the consumer, not the producer of the prop. That is why the gap
survived the first validation round.

### The fix (3 files)
- `packages/web/src/components/workspace/types.ts`: `WorkspaceEditorProps`
  gains an optional `events?: import('@shared/socket').ChatEvent[]`. Optional
  so the other six editors (doc, sheet, slides, video, loam-video, craft) keep
  compiling unchanged; the canvas is the only editor that reads it.
- `packages/web/src/components/workspace/WorkspacePanel.tsx`: forwards
  `events={events}` to the mounted editor.
- `packages/web/src/components/workspace/canvas/Editor.tsx`: destructures
  `events` and passes `events={events ?? []}` to `CanvasPanel`.

### Regression test (new)
`packages/web/src/components/workspace/canvas/__tests__/Editor.test.tsx` pins
the wrapper seam, which the panel test cannot reach. It was verified to fail
against the bug: reverting only the `Editor.tsx` line to
`<CanvasPanel taskId={file.taskId} live={live} />` makes the test report
`data-tools=""` instead of `data-tools="web_search"`, then passes again once
the fix is restored. A test that cannot fail is not evidence.

## Acceptance criteria re-checked on the real paths (unchanged, still satisfied)
- 6+ nodes live: `CanvasPanel` renders one `canvas-node` per graph node and
  lists `recipe_step` nodes in the Recipe panel; the fixture is a 7-node graph
  (root + 6 steps) and the test asserts 7 cards and `7 nodes`.
- Organize without overlap: `applyLayout` groups by `depthMap` (longest-path
  depth, cycle-safe) and spaces siblings on x and layers on y; `hasOverlaps` is
  the pinned invariant and the test asserts every card transform is distinct.
- E opens the detail: the `keydown` handler opens the newest node
  (`nodesRef.current.at(-1)`), Escape closes it, and a card click toggles it.
- RTL: `ar.json` carries the real strings (`Recipe` -> `الوصفة`, `nodes` ->
  `عقد`, `RTL` -> `من اليمين إلى اليسار`); the panel syncs the document
  direction when it owns the locale, and the surface stays `dir="ltr"`.

