## V8 gate-fix session: merge with manus-parity, all gates green

`.jgatefail.txt` reported: `MERGE CONFLICT with latest manus-parity: run git merge
manus-parity, resolve all conflicts keeping both sides, commit.`

### Root cause
No source file conflicted. `git merge manus-parity` brought the N2 canvas-view
workstream (parity tip `1ccc8bd`, the N2 merge; merge base `d57df77`): the
`WorkspaceEditorProps.events` contract in `packages/web/src/components/workspace/types.ts`,
the forwarding in `WorkspacePanel.tsx`, the `events` prop on the canvas `Editor.tsx` and the new
`canvas/__tests__/Editor.test.tsx`. Every one of those source and test files auto-merged cleanly
with `ort` against the V8 design-system change set, because the paths are disjoint
(V8 lives in `src/design/**` and `src/tools/uiExamples.ts`). The only file that conflicted was
the tracked rollup `.jdone`, because every workstream prepends its own report at the same
top-of-file anchor:

- **ours** (HEAD, `22b10f5`): the V8 validation-pass report.
- **theirs** (parity tip `1ccc8bd`): the N2 canvas report.

### Resolution
The conflicted working copy already held the full multiset union of both sides, so keeping both
sides meant removing the six conflict-marker lines only. Verified mechanically against the three
blobs in play with a line-bag check: the resolved file is missing 0 non-blank lines from the base
blob (`:1:`), 0 from ours (`:2:`) and 0 from theirs (`:3:`). No line of either side was dropped,
no conflict marker remains, the file is LF-only with no BOM, and the Arabic text is intact.

### Nothing was dropped from the merge
The merge tree is parity plus V8: for every file parity changed, the merged tree is a superset of
parity's version, and V8's own files (`src/design/registry.ts`, `src/design/retrieval.ts`,
`src/tools/uiExamples.ts`, `src/tools/__tests__/uiExamples.test.ts`) are untouched by parity.
