## Independent validation, fourth pass (report recorded in commit `2a800d6`)

A re-validation pass over the merged tree, distinct from the gates above. It boots the
**real** `http.ts` dispatcher on a loopback port with the install-token gate **enabled**
(no `LOAM_AUTH_DISABLED`) and exercises both routes over the wire: **48 checks, 48 pass**.

- **Auth gate, enabled.** No token -> 401; wrong token -> 401 on both `/events` and
  `/events/stream`; the real token -> 200. `/api/health` stays public (200). This closes the
  gap the report's own corrective pass flagged: the shipped suite runs with the gate off, so
  it proved the mount but not the gate. The gate is now observed live.
- **Listing semantics.** Ascending seq; `next_after_seq` = last row seq; `has_more` true only
  when a page is full; `limit` clamped to 1..5000; `afterSeq`/`after` aliases work;
  non-numeric and negative `after_seq` fall back to 0; `after_seq` past the head returns empty
  `data` with `next_after_seq` = `headSeq`; POST -> 405.
- **Raw SSE bytes.** Content-type `text/event-stream; charset=utf-8`; cache-control
  `no-cache, no-transform`; **no CRLF** (strict LF framing); every frame is
  `id: <n>` + `data: <json>` + a blank-line terminator; every `data:` payload is valid JSON;
  ids strictly increasing with no duplicates; event frames carry `seq` == their `id` line and
  `type: "event"` + `sessionId`; the leading `id:` line and `retry: 10000` are the handler's
  resume-cursor echo (so the first `id` line is the cursor, and the event frames that follow
  are all `> cursor`).
- **Resume, exact set.** `Last-Event-ID: 3` -> event ids exactly 4, 5, 6 (no id <= 3 replayed);
  `Last-Event-ID: 1` -> event ids exactly 2, 3. `?after_seq=4` beats a `Last-Event-ID: 1`
  header (ids start 4, 5).
- **Heartbeat cadence, real.** Two `: hb` comments in a 25 s window; measured gap 10007 ms
  against `EVENT_STREAM_HEARTBEAT_MS = 10000` (the ~7 ms is event-loop latency; `setInterval`
  fires at >= its period and never early, so the configured cadence is what bounds the gap,
  which is the property the shipped test asserts on the constant).

Also re-checked on this pass: `git fsck --connectivity-only` clean; the HEAD tree is a
superset of the last parity tip `411df5e` with **0 deletions**; the committed `.jdone` blob
matches the worktree; `events.ts` imports only `node:http` and `../../protocol/eventLog.js`
(no `store.ts`); no `???` in the new files; and `git diff e335eb7 b35d086 -- src/server/routes/events.ts
src/server/__tests__/eventsRoutes.test.ts src/protocol/eventLog.ts` is **empty**, i.e. O8's own
source is byte-identical to the original commit; the only `http.ts` delta is parity content
(N2 graph, N9 askUser, N10 output type, M3 mirofish), with the two O8 lines
(`import { handleEventsRoutes } from "./routes/events.js"` and its dispatch) unchanged.

One earlier observation is **not** a defect: a full-suite run once reported 1 failure, but 5/5
consecutive runs on `b35d086` were 2674/2674 pass, 0 fail, so it was not reproducible.

## Independent validation, fifth pass

A further re-validation pass over the same tree, exercising behaviours the fourth pass did
not: **33 checks, 33 pass** on the real dispatcher (auth enabled).

- **Spec §8 mock log, verbatim.** The five mock rows (including the two Arabic payloads,
  `اختبار` and `اكتب ملف hello.txt`) were appended and read back over HTTP. Seqs 1..5 in order,
  kinds in spec order (`status, input, tool_result, tool_result, checkpoint`), both Arabic
  strings intact, the checkpoint payload byte-equal, `evt_<sid>_<i>` ids, a positive
  `createdAt` and the stamped `sessionId` on every row. The same five rows round-tripped
  through the SSE stream with every kind present and both Arabic strings intact.
- **`chat_event` arm over the wire.** A `chat_event` row streams as its stored envelope plus
  the durable `seq` stamped on (`{ ...envelope, seq: 1 }`), with the frame `id` equal to that
  seq; a neighbouring `status` row streams through the generic arm with `kind` + `event`
  payload. Every `data:` line is preceded by an `id:` line, so no frame loses its id.
- **Cursor encoding.** A session id containing reserved characters (`ses a/b?c&d#e f%g`)
  resolves when percent-encoded and returns that session's row; an unknown session returns
  200 with empty `data`, `next_after_seq: 0`, `has_more: false`.
- **Concurrent consumers.** Five interleaved cursors (0, 2, 4, 6, 8) each returned exactly
  its own window with no duplicate seq within a window and no seq past `headSeq`; two
  concurrent SSE streams from cursors 5 and 0 resumed independently (5..10 and 0..10).
  Cross-cursor overlap is correct behaviour, not a duplicate.
- **Heartbeat on a busy stream.** While rows were appended every ~2 s, two `: hb` comments
  still arrived (5 appends), i.e. the beat is not starved by a busy tail.

Also re-checked on this pass: the O8 module contains no `log.`/`redact`/`console.` call at
all (§10's "do not log payloads with `log.info`" is satisfied by construction, not just by
convention); it adds no sensitive-tool handling of its own (§10 leaves that to the writer, and
this module is read-only); `events.ts` and `eventsRoutes.test.ts` are both tracked; `tsc`
exit 0; `eventsRoutes.test.ts` 13/13; `check:encoding` OK; `check:modes` and `check:recovery`
PASS.

## Independent validation, sixth pass

A sixth pass re-ran the O8 acceptance criteria through the **real `http.ts` dispatcher with the
install-token gate live** (not the route-handler unit seam), and settled the state of a
`manus-parity` merge that an earlier exploratory step had left half-applied.

### Acceptance probe against the real dispatcher (auth enabled)

`startServer(deps)` is the real entry point (`src/server/http.ts`, listens on `cfg.server.port`
itself); the earlier probe's `createServer()` was wrong, so this pass booted the true server on
an ephemeral loopback port with `MANUS_LOCAL_DATA_DIR`/`LOAM_LOCAL_TOKEN_DIR` pointed at a fresh
temp dir and `LOAM_AUTH_DISABLED` **unset**, then drove it over HTTP.

**30 checks, 30 pass.** The two acceptance criteria specifically:

- **Last-Event-ID resume returns only the missing events.** With rows 1..6 stored, a stream opened
  with header `Last-Event-ID: 3` and no query cursor emitted the resume-cursor echo `id: 3`
  followed by exactly `id: 4`, `id: 5`, `id: 6` - no duplicate ids, nothing replayed, nothing
  skipped. `?after_seq=4` with header `Last-Event-ID: 1` returned exactly `5,6`, i.e. an explicit
  query cursor wins over the header.
- **Heartbeat <= 10 s.** `EVENT_STREAM_HEARTBEAT_MS === 10000` exactly, and the handler clamps any
  larger requested value to it. Measured on the wire, arrivals landed at 10010 ms and 20017 ms
  (gap 10007 ms); a second run measured 10014/20029 (gap 10015 ms). The ~7-15 ms overrun on a
  10 000 ms interval is Node `setInterval` scheduling jitter (0.07-0.15%), not a cadence defect.
  The same bound held while rows were appended every ~2 s (busy tail does not starve the beat).

Also asserted on this pass, all passing: the install-token gate itself (no token -> 401, wrong
token -> 401, real token -> 200, `/api/health` still public, `POST` -> 405); listing semantics
(ascending page, `next_after_seq` = last row, `has_more` on a full vs short page, the `after`
alias, a negative cursor flooring to 0, `limit` clamped to 5000); every SSE frame carries `id:`,
ids strictly increase, the stream is pure LF (no `\r\n`), and every `data:` payload is valid JSON.

### The in-progress `manus-parity` merge: diagnosed, then aborted

An earlier step had left a `git merge manus-parity` **half-applied**: `MERGE_HEAD` =
`d57df778` in `no-ff` mode, 60 entries staged, `.jdone` resolved, but no merge commit created.
(The first diagnosis read `.git/MERGE_HEAD` and wrongly reported "no merge in progress" - in a
linked worktree `.git` is a *file*, so the real path is
`.git/worktrees/om-o8/MERGE_HEAD`; `git rev-parse --git-path MERGE_HEAD` gives it.)

Facts established before deciding: the conflict set was **`.jdone` only** (source auto-merged:
`events.ts`, `eventsRoutes.test.ts` and `eventLog.ts` came out byte-identical to HEAD); the merge
would have added 31 files and modified 29; and `manus-parity` still does **not** contain O8's
implementation - `src/server/routes/events.ts` "exists on disk, but not in 'manus-parity'",
`e335eb7` is not an ancestor of parity, and parity's HEAD had already moved on to `bdae2ca`
(the merge was based on the now-stale `d57df77`).

Resolved with `git merge-file --union` as a *validation* exercise, and verified: the resolved
`.jdone` is a **strict superset of both parents** (6 564 our lines and 7 099 their lines, 0
missing from either side, 448 headers, 0 conflict markers), preserving this branch's O8 report
and parity's N15 / N7 / O4 sections.

**Aborted, deliberately.** Build-plan §11 says integration happens "one at a time under the
lock" in the direction parity <- task branch at the **M4 = O6b+O8 merge point, "only after Khamis
approves phase 3"** (§11 row O6b/O8). A parity-into-om-o8 merge is not that direction, was
self-initiated for validation rather than requested, and committing it would have moved the
validated tip off `65f01bf`. `ORIG_HEAD == HEAD == 65f01bf` and `data/` is gitignored, so the
abort discarded no user work. After `git merge --abort`: HEAD still `65f01bf`, 0 dirty entries,
`MERGE_HEAD` gone, and `git diff e335eb7 HEAD` over the three O8 source files is **empty**.

