# J1 - Shared agent server spike: DONE

Summary
-------
Loam's coding launcher paid one heavyweight `node --import tsx` process per coding
task. J1 measures that BEFORE shape against the AFTER shape (one long-lived agent
server hosting N concurrent sessions over a control socket), lands the AFTER shape
as a selectable `code_session` launcher, and commits the numbers.

The AFTER shape is production code (`src/server/sharedCodeSession.ts`) and is
exposed as `launcher: "shared"` on the `code_session` tool
(`src/tools/codeSession.ts`). The default is unchanged (`per-process`), because
the task spec allows the default to stay unless sharing is clearly better, and
sharing is opt-in via `LOAM_CODE_SESSION_LAUNCHER=shared`.

Files
-----
- `src/server/sharedCodeSession.ts`  - the AFTER launcher: one long-lived server, control socket, N sessions.
- `src/tools/codeSession.ts`         - `launcher` option + `SharedCodeSessionServer` (one server, many sessions).
- `bench/launchers.ts`               - measures both shapes against the same fixture and fake model.
- `bench/perProcess.ts`              - the BEFORE launcher (one process per session).
- `bench/rssSampler.ts`              - process-tree working-set / PSS sampler.
- `bench/results/J1-before.json`, `bench/results/J1-after.json`, `bench/results/J1.json`.
- `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES`              - jcode MIT notice entries for the ported bench code.

Measured RAM numbers (win32, scripted fake model, offline, all sessions fixed)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
BEFORE, one heavyweight process per session (`bench/results/J1-before.json`):

| N  | idle MB | peak MB | final MB | perSession MB | marginal MB/session |
|----|---------|---------|----------|---------------|---------------------|
| 1  | 249.1   | 409.5   | 253.1    | 160.4         | n/a (baseline)      |
| 10 | 248.8   | 1523.0  | 273.3    | 127.4         | 123.7               |
| 30 | 249.1   | 2476.7  | 292.2    | 74.3          | 71.3                |

AFTER, one shared server hosting every session (`bench/results/J1-after.json`):

| N  | idle MB | peak MB | final MB | perSession MB | marginal MB/session |
|----|---------|---------|----------|---------------|---------------------|
| 1  | 248.5   | 421.7   | 421.7    | 173.2         | n/a (baseline)      |
| 10 | 248.8   | 471.8   | 471.8    | 22.3          | 5.6                 |
| 30 | 248.6   | 512.3   | 512.3    | 8.8           | 3.1                 |

`marginal MB/session` is `(peakMB - baselineMB) / (N - 1)`, i.e. what each
*additional* session costs once the launcher is already running. At N=30 the
shared launcher costs **3.1 MB per additional session**, against **71.3 MB** for
the per-process shape: a ~23x reduction, and the peak is nearly flat
(512.3 MB at N=30 vs 421.7 MB at N=1, for 30x the work).

Acceptance criteria (all met)
-----------------------------
- `bench/results/J1-before.json` and `J1-after.json` committed, N=1/10/30. DONE.
- Marginal session cost < 10 MB in shared mode: **3.1 MB at N=30, 5.6 MB at
  N=10**. DONE.
- All sessions fix the task: **30/30** in both shapes at every N. DONE.
- Tests for the launcher: `bench/__tests__/launchers.test.ts` (14 tests),
  `src/server/__tests__/sharedCodeSession.test.ts`,
  `src/tools/__tests__/codeSession.test.ts` (shared-launcher cases). DONE.
- Gates pass (below). DONE.

Two measurement bugs found and fixed (the numbers above are the corrected ones)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
The first committed run measured the two shapes in one process, and the AFTER
numbers described the measurement order rather than the launcher:

1. **Process sharing.** Interleaving both shapes lets V8 grow the shared server's
   heap in response to the per-process run's ~2.5 GB pressure: a standalone shared
   N=30 peaks ~515 MB, but ~1500 MB when measured in the same process as the
   per-process runs. Every measurement now runs in its own child process
   (`runIsolatedMeasurement`, `--isolate <kind>` + `--report-out`), on by default
   via `runJ1Bench({ isolateEach: true })`. A child that crashes still writes a
   failure report instead of hanging.

2. **Truncated sampling window.** `--sample-ms` (default 4000) *capped* the
   sampler, but N=30 spends ~9s settling its 30 sessions one by one and peaks part
   way through, so its peak was cut off at 1493 MB instead of the real 2477 MB. The
   window is now a backstop (`MAX_SAMPLE_WINDOW_MS`) and sampling stops as soon as
   the run's work is done.

Both guards are covered by tests, and `bench/README.md` documents them as the
primary way to keep the AFTER number a property of the launcher.

Test commands
-------------
    npx tsc --noEmit
    npm run build:server
    (cd packages/web && npx next build)
    npm run test:bench
    node --import tsx --test src/server/__tests__/sharedCodeSession.test.ts src/tools/__tests__/codeSession.test.ts
    (cd packages/web && npx vitest run)
    npm run check:encoding && npm run check:modes && npm run check:orchestrator && npm run check:promptwire
    npm run bench:j1 -- --n 1,10,30 --before-out bench/results/J1-before.json --after-out bench/results/J1-after.json

