# N5 round 6: parity N16 merged, and a mis-reported figure caught

## A figure I reported was wrong, and why

In round 5 this file recorded "focused N5 ... 77 tests, 77 pass". That number is **not
reproducible from the command as I ran it**: `node --import tsx --test <five files>` prints
`tests 77` on a clean re-run, but the *first* time I ran the same command it printed
`tests 50`. The cause is not flakiness in the tests and not duplicate-name skipping:

- per file the counts are exact and stable: `contextSelector.test.ts` 26, `contextSelectorLongHorizon.test.ts` 5, `runGraph.test.ts` 27, `loopBudget.test.ts` 6, `loopHooks.test.ts` 13, summing to **77**;
- the two N5 files alone report `tests 31` (= 26 + 5);
- the combined run reports `tests 77`, `skipped 0`, `cancelled 0`, so nothing was skipped.

So the suite is deterministic at 77 and the `50` reading was a measurement artifact of that
one invocation (the output was truncated by the pipe), not a property of the code. The
lesson recorded here: **a single truncated run is not evidence, and the per-file sum is the
check that catches it.** The figure in round 5 was asserted from a run whose output I did
not read to the end; it happens to match the real value, but it was not verified when
written. This round re-verified it three ways.

## Parity advanced twice; merged the real one

`git fetch origin manus-parity` moved the remote-tracking ref to `0a946d3` ("Merge main
(packaging asar+fuses fix, 0.5.28) into manus-parity"), but the **local** `manus-parity` ref
had already moved to `7b75243` ("merge `khamis1992/neo-n16` (N16) into manus-parity"). The
two are not the same line: the local ref has 438 commits the remote lacks, and the remote
ref is an ancestor of the local ref, i.e. **the local ref is ahead and the remote is behind.**

Concretely: `git merge origin/manus-parity` said "Already up to date" because `origin/manus-parity`
(=`0a946d3`) was already an ancestor of HEAD. The work that actually needs merging is the
local `manus-parity` = N16, merged here as `061c5a3`.

**N16 does not touch N5.** The N16 diff is 13 files, +1580/-5: `src/graph/recall.ts` (+645),
`src/graph/__tests__/recall.test.ts` (+414), `src/graph/runGraph.ts` (+127), `src/tools/memory.ts`
(+131), `src/server/runTools.ts`, `src/tools/registry.ts`, `src/index.ts`, `src/setup/runtime.ts`,
`src/agent/insights.ts`, `src/agent/runGraphAdapter.ts`, `src/agent/sideChat.ts`,
`src/server/__tests__/runTools.test.ts`, `.jdone`. N16's own files (`recall.ts`, `memory.ts`)
do not overlap N5's, and its `runGraph.ts` change is additive dispatch wiring that auto-merged
in a disjoint region from N5's `case "context_selected":` handler.

The merge was conflict-free (`Auto-merging .jdone`, `Auto-merging src/graph/runGraph.ts`, then
"Merge made by the 'ort' strategy"), so the union driver was not even needed this time.

## N5 wiring re-verified after the merge (all five points present)

| Point | Location |
| --- | --- |
| selector imported and constructed | `src/agent/loop.ts:29` (`import { ContextSelector }`), `:517` (`opts.contextSelector ?? new ContextSelector(...)`) |
| option plumbed | `src/agent/loop.ts:212` (`contextSelector?: ContextSelector`) |
| event emitted | `src/agent/loop.ts:595` (`opts.emit({ type: "context_selected", step, tokens, artefacts, reason })`) |
