## Seams left for other workstreams

- The shelf is embedded with the **memory** embedder only. A workstream that adds a
  dedicated embedding model or a remote embedding service can swap it in through
  `RecallIndexOptions.embedder` without touching the indexing logic.
- `attachRecallNode` files hits as a `note` node. A canvas view that wants to render
  recalled assets with their own card (image/video preview, a "from run X" badge)
  can read `data.recalled` / `data.sourceRunId` off that node.
- The shelf caps nodes through `maxNodes` (0 = unlimited, the current default). A
  retention policy belongs with the run-graph retention work, not here.
- `recall` is not in the web canvas UI yet; the tools and the node link are the
  contract a view would consume.

