## The one remaining node failure (pre-existing, environmental, not caused by this merge)
`src/server/__tests__/worktrees.test.ts` -> "reports non-git folders without
throwing" (`true == false` at `src/server/__tests__/worktrees.test.ts:44`).
Neither `src/server/__tests__/worktrees.test.ts` nor `src/server/worktrees.ts`
is touched by this merge (`git diff` of both between the pre-merge HEAD and the
merged HEAD is empty), and the cause is environmental: `%TEMP%` on this machine is
`C:\Users\khamis\AppData\Local\Temp`, and `git -C %TEMP% rev-parse` walks up and
resolves to `C:/Users/khamis`, which is itself a git repository, so a fresh temp
folder is reported as a git folder. Confirmed by a direct probe in this session.

No secrets committed. No forbidden path touched. No test weakened, deleted or
skipped. No `.neo-*` or `.jcode-*` marker file was staged. Working tree clean.
## Root cause
No source file conflicted on the first merge. `git merge manus-parity` (tip
`ed26550`, the N2 merge, bringing in N10/N2/N4/C19/O3/O6/O2/D5/O1/V11/H0/O0/fc-05/
J5/F5) auto-merged everything except the tracked rollup `.jdone`, where both sides
prepend a report at the same top-of-file anchor. Nothing in the C20 change set was
at risk: `git diff manus-parity -- ui/` still shows exactly the C20 files
(`ui/chat-color.js`, `ui/chat-color.d.ts`, `ui/app.js`, `ui/companions.js`,
`ui/companions.html`, `ui/loam.css`, `ui/styles.css`, 712 insertions / 9 deletions).

