## H3 gate-fix session note (2026-10-23, third merge of manus-parity)
`.jgatefail.txt` reported: MERGE CONFLICT with latest manus-parity. The only conflicted
file was the tracked rollup marker `.jdone` (add/add: this branch's C19/H3 reports vs
parity's O3/O6/O2/D5/O1/V11/fc-05/N9 rollup). No source file conflicted and no source
file was edited: the H3 deliverables are unchanged from commit `f40f2d9` and the parity
O1 deliverables are unchanged from commit `83b6b8a`.
Resolution method: for each conflict hunk, emit the true superset of both sides as a
multiset union, capping each distinct line at `max(count in HEAD, count in manus-parity)`,
preserving the order A -> B -> tail. This keeps every line of both sides while eliminating
genuine duplication from the shared region.
Two successive parity tips were merged and resolved (parity advanced mid-fix):
1. `a61bc30` Merge manus-parity (tip `0a946d3`) - containment missing 0, duplication 0.
2. `0c6e64b` Merge manus-parity (tip `61aca0c`) - containment missing 0, duplication 0.
A third `git merge manus-parity` now reports "Already up to date."
Integrity of the resolved rollup: containment missing 0 vs HEAD, 0 vs manus-parity, 0 vs
BASE; genuine duplication (beyond the union cap) 0; conflict markers 0; no CRLF, no BOM,
no mojibake. The one remaining "orphaned heading" (`## Preserved: manus-parity .jdone
rollup ...`) is parity's own structure (present verbatim in manus-parity, absent from
HEAD), so it is preserved by design.
