`.jgatefail.txt` reported: `MERGE CONFLICT with latest manus-parity in: .jdone. Run git merge
manus-parity, resolve those files keeping both sides, commit.`

### Root cause
No source file conflicted. `git merge manus-parity` (parity tip `84c9af8`, the N3 Knowledge Garden
merge) brought the N3 workstream: `src/knowledge/*` (SQLite-backed KB store, import pipeline,
chunking, importers, hybrid lexical + vector search), `src/tools/knowledge.ts` (the `kb_*` tool
set), `src/server/knowledgeTools.ts` and `src/server/routes/knowledge.ts`, the `GET /api/knowledge*`
routes, the per-run toggle (web `KnowledgeGardenPane.tsx`, `knowledgeApi.ts`, the `kb_seed` graph
nodes) and the N3 i18n additions. Every one of those source and test files auto-merged cleanly with
`ort` against V8's disjoint paths (`src/design/**`, `src/tools/uiExamples.ts`), because they are
separate files.

`src/index.ts` auto-merged too: V8's `createUiExamplesTools` import and `registerAll` call survive
and parity's `applyKnowledgeGate` import, the `knowledgeRunAllow` allowlist narrowing, the
`knowledge: opts.knowledge === true` field on the saved run and the `embedder: rt.embedder`
hand-off to the server all survive. No wiring was lost on either side.

The only file that conflicted was the tracked rollup `.jdone`, because every workstream prepends
its own report at the same top-of-file anchor:

- **ours** (HEAD, `db176f4`): the V8 round-10 report and the whole V8/J11 rollup below it.
- **theirs** (parity tip `84c9af8`): the N3 Knowledge Garden rollup.

### Resolution
The conflicted working copy already held the full multiset union of both sides, so keeping both
sides meant removing the conflict-marker lines only (8 `<<<<<<<`, 8 `=======` and 8 `>>>>>>>` lines).
Verified mechanically against the merge stages:

| Stage | Missing from resolved `.jdone` |
| --- | --- |
| base (`:1:`, `d1862d6`) | 0 |
