# N10 complete: output modes, effort and model map (A/B arms actually execute)

Committed as `0ea4423`. The N10 task's A/B criterion is "A/B creates 3 sibling nodes with
model labels". The nodes were being created, and the canvas showed them, but the models
behind them were never asked anything: every arm stayed `init` forever and no answer was
ever produced. This session fixed that defect, which is the part of N10 that was missing.

## The defect, located before coding

`src/agent/loop.ts` (~lines 376-395 at HEAD `851b3fe`) called `addRunSiblings(...)` and
emitted `"A/B arm started on {model}"`, then never dispatched a model call and never
transitioned the node. `git grep` confirmed no other call site ran an arm. So the recorded
graph events and the node rows were real, but the underlying models never ran: node status
stayed `init` because nothing ever set it to `running` or `finished`.

## What shipped

**1. Arms now run their own model (`src/agent/loop.ts`)**
New `runAbArm(opts, system, arm, model)`:
- sets the node `running`, then calls `chatWithFallback` with the run's own system prompt
  and the run's own `opts.prompt` under the arm's model, so failover/routing still applies;
- on success stores `{ ...existing, model: result.model, answer: oneLine(answer) }` via
  `setRunNodeData` and sets `finished`, emitting `"A/B arm finished on {result.model}."`;
- on failure stores `{ ...existing, model, error: oneLine(reason) }` and sets `failed`,
  emitting an error event. A cancelled arm is `skipped`, not `failed`, because the user
  stopped the run and the arm never had a chance to answer. `runAbArm` never rethrows.
- an arm with no model label is skipped (`if (!model) continue`) rather than silently sent
  to the config default model.

Arms are awaited in three places so no sibling is ever left pending: before the successful
`return`, before the step-budget `throw`, and at the top of `finally` (so a throwing run
still settles its arms).

**2. Tests (`src/agent/__tests__/abRouting.test.ts`, rewritten, 275 lines)**
The fake `chatClient` now takes `(model, calls[])` and records every requested model, and
arm answers read `done by ${requested}`. Four tests: (1) records one arm per model AND
runs each arm's own model, asserting both arm models were dispatched and each arm is
`finished` with its own answer; (2) a failed arm lands `failed` with an error while the run
rejects (contained); (3) `suppressFinal: true` creates no arms; (4) no arms without
`abModels`.

**3. Canvas renders the arm (`packages/web/src/components/workspace/canvas/CanvasPanel.tsx`)**
`SUBTITLE_KEYS` gained `answer` and `TITLE_KEYS` gained `model`, so an arm card shows the
model that answered and the answer it produced instead of only its status. Covered by a new
`CanvasPanel.test.tsx` case that renders two finished arms and asserts each card carries
its own model and its own answer, plus the `Model arm · Finished` kind/status line.

