## What was produced
`docs/re/harness2-H0.md` (556 lines, committed as `ea8c597`). Every claim carries a
`file:line` read from this worktree at baseline HEAD `a8130cc`. No source file was
modified; `node_modules` was excluded from all searches.
### Root cause
No source file conflicted. `git merge manus-parity` (parity tip `1ccc8bd`, the N2 canvas
merge; merge base `d57df77`) brought the N2 canvas-view workstream: the
`WorkspaceEditorProps.events` contract in `packages/web/src/components/workspace/types.ts`, the
forwarding in `WorkspacePanel.tsx`, the `events` prop on the canvas `Editor.tsx` and the new
`canvas/__tests__/Editor.test.tsx`. Every one of those source and test files auto-merged
cleanly with `ort` against V8's disjoint paths (`src/design/**`, `src/tools/uiExamples.ts`).
The only file that conflicted was the tracked rollup `.jdone`, because every workstream prepends
its own report at the same top-of-file anchor:

- **ours** (HEAD, `22b10f5`): the V8 validation-pass report.
- **theirs** (parity tip `1ccc8bd`): the N2 canvas report.

The parity ref then advanced again mid-fix, from `1ccc8bd` to `bdae2ca` (`merge
khamis1992/jcode-j11 (J11 via loam-jcode-run) into manus-parity`), carrying the J11 context
compressor, cache-usage accounting, reminders and `src/config.ts` work. That second merge was
resolved in the same way and is recorded further below, after the round-10 report.

### Resolution
For each conflict, the conflicted working copy already held the full multiset union of both
sides, so keeping both sides meant removing the conflict-marker lines only. Verified
mechanically with a line-bag check against every blob in play:

| Merge | Base (`:1:`) missing | Ours (`:2:`) missing | Theirs (`:3:`) missing |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| round 10 (`1ccc8bd`) | 0 | 0 | 0 |
| round 11 (`bdae2ca`, J11) | 0 | 0 | 0 |

