# C20 - Per-bot chat color (UI1): DONE

Each conversation now takes the color of the bot it belongs to. The user
bubble, send button and composer focus ring follow the companion's avatar
instead of the single global accent; a conversation with no bot keeps the
app accent exactly as before.
## What N3 delivered
A per-workspace knowledge base the agent can build itself and search during a run:
- `src/knowledge/` — `store.ts` (SQLite-backed bases + seeds), `ingest.ts` (import pipeline),
  `splitter.ts` (chunking), `importers.ts` (text / file / URL), `search.ts` (hybrid
  lexical + vector ranking), `text.ts`, `types.ts`.
- `src/tools/knowledge.ts` — the `kb_*` tool set (`kb_search`, `kb_ingest`, `kb_add_seed`,
  `kb_retag_seed`, `kb_delete_seed`) kept in one place (single policy module).
- `src/server/routes/knowledge.ts` — REST routes, mounted in `src/server/http.ts`,
  `src/server/recovery.ts` and `src/server/companionGateway.ts`.
- `src/server/knowledgeTools.ts` — server-side tool wiring.
- Per-run toggle: the KB is opt-in per run and surfaced in the web settings pane
  (`packages/web/src/components/settings/KnowledgeGardenPane.tsx`, added to
  `SettingsDialog.tsx` under the Capabilities group) and the API service
  (`packages/web/src/services/knowledgeApi.ts`).
- Run graph: each seed a `kb_search` actually read is emitted as a `kb_seed` node hanging
  off the `search` node (`src/graph/runGraph.ts`, `src/graph/store.ts`, `src/agent/events.ts`,
  `src/agent/loop.ts`), so the retrieved evidence is cited on the canvas.

