# J8 merge session: merge the latest manus-parity keeping both sides

`.jgatefail.txt` reported: `MERGE CONFLICT with latest manus-parity: run git merge
manus-parity, resolve all conflicts keeping both sides, commit.`

## The gate is time-sensitive: the ref moved twice under this session

`refs/heads/manus-parity` is a live branch that other workstreams keep merging
into, so "latest manus-parity" is a moving target. The gate condition is
`git merge-base --is-ancestor manus-parity HEAD` (exit 0), which is only true for
the CURRENT tip, so a merge against a stale snapshot fails the gate even though
it is internally consistent. Three tips were involved here:

  * `d05e4b1` -> `045f3e2` -> `cf45585` -> `0a946d3`: the ref advanced while an
    earlier attempt at this merge was still in progress. That attempt had merged
    a stale snapshot, which silently DROPPED parity-only files and their wiring
    (`src/server/inputQueue.ts` + 2 suites, the `src/policy/commandRisk/` package
    + 4 suites, `src/protocol/eventLogMigrate.ts` + 2 suites, neo-n4's
    `src/agent/recipe.ts` + 5 suites) because those files did not exist in the
    snapshot being merged and so were invisible to it. Aborted and re-merged
    against `0a946d3`, resolving all 7 conflicts keeping BOTH sides
    (commit `0661c47`).
  * `0a946d3` -> `ed26550` (N2: canvas view, graph routes, auto-open fix, i18n):
    advanced AGAIN while the previous commit was being finalized, so
    `merge-base --is-ancestor` flipped to exit 1 and the gate failed again.
  * This session re-merged the true current tip `ed26550`.

## The final merge (`ed26550`) had zero conflicts

Every source file auto-merged cleanly. The only staged change to a file that both
sides had touched is `.jdone` (add/add: J8's record vs parity's N2 rollup), and it
resolved automatically because the J8 side was byte-identical to parity's at
that point: parity's rollup already contained every line of this branch's report,
so keeping both sides and keeping theirs are the same file. Verified mechanically:
`git diff ed26550 -- .jdone` is empty, and the merged file is 5447 lines with the
N2 report at the top and the full parity rollup after it.

No J8 source file was edited by this merge, and no J8 addition was lost. Re-checked
every symbol the two J8 commits introduced (`58d3673` feat, `b02e220` fix), all
still present in the merged tree:

  * `src/tools/fileTouch.ts` (353 lines, new): `fileTouchRegistry`,
    `forgetFileTouchSession`, the per-session read-tracking guard and the
    large-snapshot digest logic.
  * `src/tools/readState.ts`: `recordWrite()` (fires the `write` hook that
    `readState.test.ts` asserts, alongside parity's `read` hook).
  * `src/agent/loop.ts`: the `fileTouchRegistry`/`forgetFileTouchSession` import,
    the readState touch hooks, the `subSeq` per-subagent session id.
  * `src/tools/files.ts`: `recordWrite()` on write, `forget()`/`recordWrite()` on
    `file_move`, `forget()` on `file_delete`, plus parity's `withLock`/`withLocks`.
  * `src/tools/multiEdit.ts`: parity's extracted `multiEditRun()` under `withLock`,
    with J8's `recordWrite()` in place of parity's `record()`.
  * `src/tools/subagents.ts`: parity's `SubagentStop` finally-guard plus J8's
    per-subagent `sessionId`.
  * `src/swarm/service.ts`: J8's `stageSeq` plus parity's `semantic_search` entry
    in `READ`.
  * `packages/web/public/marketplace/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES`: J8's file-touch
    attribution alongside parity's kvCacheMonitor + bench attribution.

## Gate condition verified on the final tree

  `git merge-base --is-ancestor manus-parity HEAD` -> exit 0
  `git rev-parse manus-parity` -> `ed26550e7d13074a8e7cf99407e2964c61777e81`
    (identical to `MERGE_HEAD`; the merge targeted the real current tip)
  `git diff --diff-filter=U --name-only` -> empty (no unmerged paths)
  `git grep -E "^(<{7}|={7}|>{7})( |$)"` -> no matches (no conflict markers)
  `git status --porcelain` -> clean
  all 4706 parity files present in the index (set comparison of the two trees)

## Gates (all run from the worktree root on the merged tree)

  1. npx tsc --noEmit                                  -> exit 0
  2. npm run build:server                              -> exit 0 (dist/server.cjs 19.5mb)
  3. (cd packages/web && npx tsc --noEmit)              -> exit 0
  4. (cd packages/web && npx next build)                -> exit 0 (Compiled successfully)
  5. (cd packages/web && npx vitest run)               -> 77 files / 521 tests, all pass
  6. node --import tsx --test "src/**/*.test.ts"       -> tests 2550, pass 2549, fail 1
  7. conflict-relevant suites (readState, fileTouch, fileTouchLoop, fileLock,
     multiEdit, editSchemaAlias, contextCompressor, editHints)
                                                        -> tests 83, pass 83, fail 0
  8. npm run check:encoding                            -> OK (no BOM, no mojibake, all JSON valid)
  9. npm run check:modes / check:orchestrator / check:recovery -> exit 0

The single node failure, `src/server/__tests__/worktrees.test.ts` "reports non-git
folders without throwing", is environmental and unrelated to this merge: the test
and `src/server/worktrees.ts` are byte-identical to manus-parity (`git diff
manus-parity HEAD` is empty for both), and `%TEMP%` resolves under `C:\Users\khamis`,
which is itself a git repository, so the "non-git folder" fixture sits inside a repo.
Re-running that suite with `TEMP` moved outside any repository passes 4/4.

No test was weakened, deleted or skipped. No assertion was relaxed. No source file
was edited. No secrets committed. No forbidden path touched. No mojibake or
placeholder text was written.
Proof the failure is not merge-induced (three independent checks):
  1. The test file, taskToolScope.ts and planTools.ts are byte-identical to
     97c53d7 (`git diff 97c53d7 HEAD -- <file>` is empty for each).
  2. Computed the test's full transitive relative-import closure (85 files).
     Only 2 of the 85 differ from parity at all (src/agent/events.ts,
     src/agent/prompt.ts, i.e. D17's own additions), and neither is reachable
     from the failing assertion: no file in the closure references
     suggest_plan or planTools. The assertion depends only on
     CODING_PROFILE.tools and the modules the test's own registry builds.
  3. Decisive experiment: reverted those 2 files to their parity bytes so all
     85 closure files were exactly parity's, and re-ran the test -> it still
     fails with the same assertion. Restored the files afterwards (blob hashes
     confirmed back at HEAD's).

This is a pre-existing upstream defect on manus-parity, outside D17's diff and
outside every file D17 touched. It was left untouched: "fixing" it would mean
either weakening/editing another task's (D4's) test or changing D4's production
tool profile, both of which the task rules forbid.

