   (8 parity commits still missing).
2. `git merge manus-parity` (parity tip `cf45585`, C19 failover endpoints + hermetic
   budget suite) -> merge commit `1f2b7a4`. No conflict: C19's `src/config.ts`,
   `src/__tests__/configFailover.test.ts` and `src/agent/__tests__/orchestratorBudget.test.ts`
   are disjoint from every N9 file, and the shared `.jdone` rollup auto-merged (both
   sides prepend at the same anchor, git's ort strategy produced a valid union).

After `1f2b7a4`, `git merge manus-parity` reports **"Already up to date."**,
`git merge-base --is-ancestor manus-parity HEAD` exits 0, and
`git rev-list --left-right --count manus-parity...HEAD` is `0  6` — zero parity
commits missing. `git status --porcelain` is empty and no conflict marker
(`^<{7}$`, `^={7}$`, `^>{7}$`) remains anywhere in the tree.

## N9 deliverables (unchanged by this session)

Structured clarification that pauses a run and resumes with the answers attached as
context, plus the auto-trigger the planner's low-confidence flag feeds:

- `src/tools/askUserTools.ts` — the `ask_user` agent tool (questions with options,
  `allowFile` upload flag, free-text fallback).
- `src/tools/askUserStore.ts` — durable pending-request records with a TTL,
  `waitForAskUser` that clears the record on abort so a cancelled card cannot leave
  the task's mutating tools blocked for the rest of the window.
- `src/tools/askUserGate.ts` — the fail-closed seam the orchestrator calls.
- `src/server/routes/askUser.ts` — the HTTP route the web client answers through.
- `src/agent/orchestrator.ts` — the pause/resume wiring and the auto trigger
  (`src/agent/__tests__/askUserAutoTrigger.test.ts` covers the vague-prompt fixture
  producing an ask node **before any tool call**).
- `src/protocol/{types,events,socket}.ts` + `src/agent/events.ts` — the
  `askUserRequested` / `askUserResolved` event pair and the `resolve_ask_user`
  client message, carried over the socket bridge
  (`src/protocol/__tests__/askUserSocket.test.ts`).
- `src/graph/runGraph.ts` — the ask node on the run graph, mirroring
  `approval_required`.
- `packages/web/src/components/approval/AskUserCard.tsx` — the right-panel card
  (auto-opens when the event arrives, user can edit or continue from chat),
  Arabic/RTL via `dir="auto"` and `packages/web/src/i18n/{en,ar}.json`.
- Registration: `src/index.ts`, `src/setup/runtime.ts`, `src/modes/catalog.ts`
  (`ask_user` in the mode-catalog CONTROL set), `prompts/loam-master.md` and
  `src/agent/masterPromptText.ts` (regenerated).

Acceptance criteria are covered by passing automated tests: the vague-prompt fixture
produces an ask node before any tool call (`askUserAutoTrigger.test.ts`), and an
answer plus an attached file resumes the run and the file is used as context
(`askUser.test.ts` + `AskUserCard.test.tsx`, the latter via vitest +
@testing-library because the Playwright harness is unavailable here).

