## N18 session note (2026-10-23): real Playwright acceptance spec, plus two browser-only bug fixes

Branch `khamis1992/neo-n18`, off `manus-parity`. Commit `9f28ce1` (7 files, +571/-8) on
top of `eb0fbdf`.

The N18 acceptance row asks for Playwright per control, and Playwright does run in this
harness, so the flow is now asserted in Chromium against a mock Loam server instead of
only through the DOM. The stale claim in `__tests__/panel.test.tsx` that Playwright is
unavailable here is corrected to point at the real spec.

Root-causing why the canvas rendered blank in the browser surfaced two real application
bugs, both of which vitest could not see because it runs on Node:

1. **Unbound `fetch`.** `client.ts`, `annotationsClient.ts` and `stream.ts` each defaulted
   to a bare `fetch` stored on the client. It is later called as a method, so `this` becomes
   the client and a browser throws `pageerror: Illegal invocation`. Node undici ignores its
   receiver, so every unit test still passed. All three now wrap the global in an arrow.
2. **Dropped placement.** `coerceCanvasNode` stripped `x`/`y`/`depth`, so every card was
   rendered at `translate(NaNpx, NaNpx)`, which a browser discards as invalid, leaving an
   empty canvas. Added `coerceCanvasLayoutNode` (a `finiteOr` helper falls back to `0` for
   missing or non-finite fields) and switched `coerceCanvasLayout` to it.

Spec details that only a real browser run revealed:
- The socket namespace ack must match the **prefix**: the client sends
  `40{"token":"e2e-token"}`, not a bare `40`.
- The mock `json(route, body, status)` helper returns `Promise<boolean>`, so the
