# N19 - Master-prompt section for Recipe mode: DONE

Commit `3094fb0` on `khamis1992/neo-n19` (base `manus-parity` at `eb17ea0`).
Depends on N4 + N9, both already merged into `manus-parity`.

## What shipped
- `prompts/loam-master.md` (+73): an original **§25 "Long-Horizon Missions (Recipe mode)"**
  with subsections 25.1-25.8. Nothing is copied from Flowith; the wording is written for
  Loam and describes the real harness:
  - 25.1 the seed is a hypothesis, not a contract (executed steps are evidence; the recipe
    wins over the frozen plan);
  - 25.2 incremental planning discipline (plan the next step, atomic + checkable steps,
    the last step is always delivery, a failed tool is information, drop dead steps, keep
    `remaining_estimate` honest, no meta-work steps);
  - 25.3 when to ask vs keep working (local/reversible R0-R1 defaults vs blocking
    `ask_user`; ask once in batch; never ask for progress);
  - 25.4 when to fan out (right grain: `spawn_agent` / `delegate_to_child` / `delegate_subagent` / `code_session`
    / `wide_research` / `deep_research`; self-contained branch briefs; respect
    `{{max_parallel_agents}}`, depth and budget; integrate like a reviewer);
  - 25.5 citing seeds, steps and evidence (recipe `id`s survive replans, run-graph node ids,
    `file:line`, evidence in `{{project_path}}/.loam/runs/<run-id>/`);
  - 25.6 budget awareness (know the ceiling, spend on the critical path, warn at ~80%,
    stop cleanly at the ceiling, charge planning to the budget);
  - 25.7 the completion node (created by the terminal `done` event; finish only through
    `finish`, which runs `.loam/verify.json`; on `blocked` leave a resumable state);
  - 25.8 mission hygiene (`progress.md`, live step status, restart-from-step is a user
    action not a retry, clean up, report at each phase or ~10-15 min, not per step).
- `src/agent/masterPrompt.ts`: `MISSION_SECTION_ID = "25"` and `missionSection()`.
  **§25 is deliberately outside `MASTER_ORDER`** - the same precedent as Appendix C
  (`CODING_MODE_SECTION_ID`), which `codingPrompt.test.ts` already documents as
  intentionally unassembled. A plain chat or build run therefore never pays for the
  mission rules.
- `src/agent/orchestrator.ts`: `missionSuffix(cfg)` = `fillMasterSlots(missionSection(),
  deriveMasterSlots(cfg))`, appended to the worker system suffix **only when
  `recipeMode`**. Filling here means no raw `{{slot}}` can reach the model.
- `src/agent/masterPromptText.ts`: regenerated via `npm run gen:master-prompt` (28 sections).

## A correctness fix made while authoring
The first draft of 25.4 named `map_reduce` and `delegate_subagent` for fan-out. Measuring the repo's own resolution path (`resolveCompanionCapabilities` + `mergeAlwaysOnTools` + `registry.forAllowlist`, across every Loam mode x work mode) showed the two are not alike:
`map_reduce` is **unreachable**: it exists as a tool object (`src/tools/mapReduce.ts:76`) and is returned by `createSpecAliasTools`, but that function is never called by the runtime, `map_reduce` is in no mode-catalog or work-mode allowlist and it is not in `ALWAYS_ON_TOOLS` (`src/server/runTools.ts`), so no run can call it.
`delegate_subagent` is the opposite case and is **reachable**: it is registered at startup (`src/setup/runtime.ts:122`) and granted by the `team` work mode (`src/server/companionGateway.ts:34`), so §25.4 names it.
`code_session`, `wide_research` and `deep_research` are the other reachable fan-out tools. The test asserts `map_reduce` never appears.
§25.4 names only reachable tools.

## Facts checked against the code before they were written into the prompt
- completion node `done:${seq}` -> `type: "complete"` (`src/graph/runGraph.ts:508-509`);
- `message` semantics (`src/tools/specAliases.ts:409`);
- the `finish` gate reads `.loam/verify.json` (`src/tools/finishTools.ts:19`);
- `ask_user` (`src/tools/askUserGate.ts:25`);
- budget badge `budget.percent` (`src/server/sessionRuntime.ts:189`; asserted at
  `src/server/__tests__/sessionRuntime.test.ts:180`);
- the R0-R1 tiers of §16 and the §19 milestone rule ("each phase, or every ~10-15 minutes of autonomous work").

## Acceptance tests (automated, all passing)
- `src/agent/__tests__/codingPrompt.test.ts`: new suite "long-horizon mission prompt
  section (N19)" asserts §25 is authored in the asset but **not** in `MASTER_ORDER`,
  that `buildMasterPrompt` does not emit it, that it renders with its heading, that all
  nine required rules are present, that it names only reachable tools, and that
  `fillMasterSlots` leaves no placeholder behind.
- `src/agent/__tests__/orchestratorRecipe.test.ts`: new e2e with the mock model. The
  harness now records the system prompt of every model turn. The test runs the same
  fixture twice - once with `recipeMode: true`, once with `recipeMode: false` - and
  asserts every recipe-mode worker receives `## 25. Long-Horizon Missions (Recipe mode)`
  with all slots filled and the workspace path substituted, while **no** turn of the plain
  run receives §25. This is the ask/fanout/complete proof the task asked for, driven by a
  mock model only (no real API).
- `src/tools/__tests__/promptwire.test.ts` + `coding-prompt.snap.json`: the section-id
  index is now 25 numbered sections followed by `appendix-a`/`b`/`c` at 25/26/27.

