## N21 merge-conflict gate fix: re-merged manus-parity (tip `6e17246`), `.jdone` resolved keeping both sides

The task's own work (`af1b981`) and its report (`a41cfdf`) were already committed;
the only failure was the recurring `MERGE CONFLICT with latest manus-parity in:
.jdone` gate. Commit `0d23354` on `khamis1992/neo-n21`.

### Root cause

`.jdone` and `.jcode-done` are append-only runner rollups that every worktree
edits independently and merges back into `manus-parity`, which keeps an
equivalent file of its own. `.gitattributes` declares `merge=union` for them,
but `manus-parity` (tip `6e17246`) carries no `.gitattributes` at all, so its side
was not union-driven and the 3-way merge produced a content conflict on
`.jdone` alone. The other 199 files auto-merged cleanly.

The two sides were in fact disjoint. `manus-parity`'s side is the J1/J11/O1/H3/
N19/N3/F6/M3 rollup (~39.6k lines) whose own
`## Preserved: manus-parity rollup (O1 gate-fix report)` header is the base's
first heading; this branch's side is the same base plus this branch's
`N3 gate-fix session` reports and the N21 Arabic/RTL report.

Mechanically verified before resolving: the base (18,949 lines) is contained in
**both** sides (0 lines of base missing from ours, 0 from theirs), and the
conflict hunk is exactly three marker lines (`<<<<<<< HEAD`, `=======`,
`>>>>>>> manus-parity`) wrapped around the two report blocks.

### Resolution

Removed only the three conflict-marker lines, keeping **both** blocks. No report,
line or separator was dropped and no test was weakened, deleted or skipped. The
result is a superset of both parents and stays an append-only rollup.

### Verification (all run from the worktree root on the merged tree)

- `git merge manus-parity` -> "Already up to date." (no conflict on a fresh merge)
- `git merge-base --is-ancestor manus-parity HEAD` -> exit 0
- `git grep -n "^<<<<<<<\|^=======$\|^>>>>>>>\|^|||||||" -- src packages` -> empty
- `npx tsc --noEmit`                                   -> exit 0
- `(cd packages/web && npx tsc --noEmit)`              -> exit 0
- `npm run build:server`                               -> exit 0 (bundle + pdf worker)
- `(cd packages/web && npx next build)`                -> exit 0 (25/25 static pages)
- `node --import tsx --test "src/**/*.test.ts"`       -> 3077 pass / 0 fail / 1 skip
      (the one skip is the pre-existing win32 guard in
       `src/server/__tests__/sharedCodeSession.test.ts:240`)
- `(cd packages/web && npx vitest run)`                -> 92 files / 639 tests, all pass
- `npm run check:encoding`                             -> OK (no BOM, no mojibake)
- `git status --porcelain`                             -> clean

### N21 acceptance tests (re-confirmed on the merged tree)

| Suite | Result |
| --- | --- |
| `src/knowledge/__tests__/arabic.test.ts` | 14 pass |
| `src/knowledge/__tests__/arabicPdf.test.ts` | 9 pass (real pdfjs worker, real Identity-H PDF) |
| `src/server/__tests__/knowledgeRoutes.test.ts` | 15 pass |
| `packages/web/.../canvas/__tests__/layout.test.ts` | 16 pass |
