The Arabic PDF acceptance path still builds a real one-page Identity-H PDF and
drives the real importer, splitter and pdfjs worker: the text extracts in
logical order, imports as seeds that split on their own sentence marks, and is
stored folded so `الفوترة` and `الفاتورة` are one retrievable term.

Playwright is not available in this harness, so the RTL screenshot review is
covered by the vitest component tests (`CanvasPanel.test.tsx` asserts the row
mirrors from the right under `rtl`, that an Arabic locale mirrors by default, that
an explicit `ltr` override still wins, and that a single-node layer is not
mirrored). `packages/web/e2e/specs/rtl.spec.ts` remains committed for a harness
that has Playwright.

### Seams left for other workstreams

- The canvas layout is direction-pinnable per panel via `layoutOptions.direction`;
  a workspace-wide RTL toggle that feeds it is still open.
- `kb_search`/`kb_ingest`/`kb_manage` already run the bilingual scorer, so no
  tool-side change was needed.
- The PDF path folds text on extraction; a future RTL HTML/office importer should
  route through the same `normalizeText` to stay consistent.
- The `.gitattributes` `merge=union` driver is not present on `manus-parity`, so
  this `.jdone` conflict recurs on every parity advance until parity carries the
  driver. Adding `.gitattributes` (`.jdone`/`.jcode-done merge=union`) to
  `manus-parity` is the durable fix and is outside this worktree's scope.
